 as models: understanding the 'Lingua Franca' of the human genome project.</article-title><source>Philosophy of science</source><year>2001</year><volume>68</volume><fpage>S251</fpage><lpage>S261</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1086/392913</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Amaral</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Scala</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Barthelemy</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Stanley</surname><given-names>HE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Classes of small-world networks</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><year>2000</year><volume>97</volume><fpage>11149</fpage><lpage>11152</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11005838</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.200327197</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pareto</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><source>Cours e'economique politique</source><year>1897</year><publisher-name>London, Macmillan</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gabaix</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Zipf's law and the growth of cities</article-title><source>American Economic Association Papers &#x00026; Proceedings</source><year>1999</year><volume>89</volume><fpage>129</fpage><lpage>132</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Barabasi</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>Albert</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Emergence of scaling in random networks</article-title><source>Science</source><year>1999</year><volume>286</volume><fpage>509</fpage><lpage>512</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10521342</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1126/science.286.5439.509</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Huberman</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name><name><surname>Adamic</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Internet - Growth dynamics of the World-Wide Web</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>1999</year><volume>401</volume><fpage>131</fpage><lpage>131</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10490019</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Buchanan</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><source>Small World</source><year>2002</year><publisher-name>Wiedenfeld &#x00026; Nicholson</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rousseau</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Rousseau</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>LOTKA: a program to fit a power law distribution to observed frequency data</article-title><source>Cybermetrics</source><year>2000</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>Paper 4</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Newman</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Clustering and preferential attachment in growing networks</article-title><source>Phys Rev E Stat Nonlin Soft Matter Phys</source><year>2001</year><volume>64</volume><fpage>025102</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11497639</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dorogovtsev</surname><given-names>SN</given-names></name><name><surname>Mendes</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Samukhin</surname><given-names>AN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Structure of growing networks with preferential linking</article-title><source>Phys Rev Lett</source><year>2000</year><volume>85</volume><fpage>4633</fpage><lpage>4636</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11082614</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1103/PhysRevLett.85.4633</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Krogh</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Process of Physiology</article-title><source>Am J Physiol</source><year>1929</year><volume>90</volume><fpage>243</fpage><lpage>251</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Krebs</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The August Krogh Principle: "For many problems there is an animal on which it can be most conveniently studied"</article-title><source>J Exp Zool</source><year>1975</year><volume>194</volume><fpage>221</fpage><lpage>226</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">811756</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/jez.1401940115</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nirei</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Souma</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Two factor model of income distribution dynamics</article-title><source>Complexity Digest: SFI Working Papers</source><year>2004</year><volume>DOI: SFI-WP 04-10-029</volume></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Medicine</surname><given-names>NL</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.nlm.nih.gov/pubs/techbull/nd02/nd02_2003_medline_data_changes.html"/></citation></ref><ref id="B29"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Meyer</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Genome Sequencing vs. Moore's Law: Cyber Challenges for the Next Decade</article-title><source>CTWatch Quarterly</source><year>2006</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>2</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B30"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zipf</surname><given-names>GK</given-names></name></person-group><source>Human behaviour and the principle of least effort: an introduction to human ecology</source><year>1949</year><publisher-name>Cambridge MA, Addison-Wesley</publisher-name></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>